Walk the member list safely while the autoformat edge filter removes from it.

gnm_auto_fmt_filter_edges drops the members that style an edge the user
turned off (the AutoFormat dialog's Settings menu) with g_slist_remove
inside a for loop that then reads ptr->next from the freed node, a use
after free that crashes the first time an edge is unchecked.  Found
through the Cocoa front end on 2026-10-13; the GTK dialog runs the same
code.  Take the next node before the body.

--- a/src/format-template.c	2026-10-13 07:05:00
+++ b/src/format-template.c	2026-10-13 07:05:00
@@ -775,12 +775,13 @@
-	GSList *ptr;
+	GSList *ptr, *next;
 	GnmFT *ft = gnm_ft_clone (origft);
 	gboolean is_edge, l = FALSE, r = FALSE, t = FALSE, b = FALSE;
 
-	for (ptr = ft->members; ptr != NULL ; ptr = ptr->next) {
+	for (ptr = ft->members; ptr != NULL ; ptr = next) {
 		GnmFTMember *member = ptr->data;
+		next = ptr->next;
 		if (member->direction != FREQ_DIRECTION_NONE)
 			continue;
 
 		is_edge = FALSE;
 		if (member->col.size == 1) {
